## Model card

- Primary NVIDIA announcement explicitly distinguishes **Bolt74B-A9B24GB available now** from **BoltE4B4GB comingOctober23**.[1] This report is datedOctober22 and does not treat scheduled release as completed.
- Primary describes physical/conversational agents on RTX/Jetson/Spark, including local voice-assistant applications. Exact native input/output modalities, context/output, parameters and cutoff are not published in the checked evidence. A voice-assistant use case does not alone establish native speech I/O.
- **4GB is the advertised footprint**, not proof of4B parameters or a tested memory figure. No exact weight license/current API/free tariff established; sibling OpenMDW terms or free local operation are not assumed.
- Publisher-scoped HF search currently finds only74B variants; models.dev and current NVIDIA serving catalog have no exact E4B record. These are bounded observations, not denial of the announcement.[2][3][4]

